  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $\\cos \\left(2 \\cos ^{-1} x+\\sin ^{-1} x\\right)$ at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QarHz",
      "text": "$-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{6}}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fnG54",
      "text": "$-2 \\sqrt{6}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6O18C",
      "text": "$-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a9jEf",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\cos \\left[2 \\cos ^{-1} x+\\sin ^{-1} x\\right]$\r\n\r\n$=\\cos \\left[\\cos ^{-1} x+\\cos ^{-1} x+\\sin ^{-1} x\\right]$\r\n\r\n$=\\cos \\left[\\cos ^{-1} x+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]=-\\sin \\left[\\cos ^{-1} x\\right]$\r\n\r\n$=-\\sin \\left[\\sin ^{-1} \\sqrt{1-x^{2}}\\right]=-\\sqrt{1-x^{2}}$\r\n\r\n$=-\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{2}}=-\\sqrt{\\frac{24}{25}}=-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{6}}{5}$",
    "image": null
  },
